  "limitations": [
    "The seven existing national Regions remain broad named physiographic regions. They must not be relabelled as smaller ranges, grassland extent, elevation observations or administrative boundaries.",
    "Rockies uses the individual Rocky Mountains Division, not the broader Cordillera Region or Rocky Mountain Area Subregion; the separately named Rocky Mountain Foothills Division is excluded.",
    "The eight selections are hierarchical and do not form an eight-way partition. Rocky Mountains overlaps its parent Cordillera by design.",
    "Interior Plains includes northern plains as well as its southern part. It is not an exact Prairies polygon. No Prairies boundary is inferred from provinces, a latitude cut or adjacent unnamed divisions.",
    "Label anchors are cartographic positions verified inside each source feature; they are not observation locations.",
    "Catalogue publication, temporal coverage and catalogue modification dates are distinct. The separately linked historical map does not establish a reference year for these vectors."
  ]
